# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Reduce the effects of noise and errors {#reduce-the-effects-of-noise-and-errors}"
msgstr "Bawasan ang mga epekto ng noise at mga error {#reduce-the-effects-of-noise-and-errors}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Several Qiskit addons focus specifically on reducing the impact of noise and hardware imperfections.\n"
msgstr "Ilang Qiskit addon ang partikular na nakatuon sa pagbabawas ng epekto ng noise at mga di-perpektong hardware.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Operator backpropagation and noise-aware circuit transformations {#operator-backpropagation-and-noise-aware-circuit-transformations}"
msgstr "Operator backpropagation at noise-aware na mga circuit transformation {#operator-backpropagation-and-noise-aware-circuit-transformations}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We have already discussed operator propagation in the context of coherent Pauli checks in error correction. However, operator propagation is useful more generally. There are two main ways to use the propagation of an operator through a quantum circuit: (1) absorb the last few layers of a quantum circuit into the observables being measured, and (2) take into account the likely effects of errors in the circuit, and compensate for them by measuring a different observable. The next two tools use these approaches.\n"
msgstr "Tinalakay na natin ang operator propagation sa konteksto ng coherent Pauli check sa error correction. Gayunpaman, kapaki-pakinabang ang operator propagation sa mas pangkalahatang paraan. May dalawang pangunahing paraan ng paggamit sa propagation ng isang operator sa isang quantum circuit: (1) sipsipin ang huling ilang layer ng isang quantum circuit sa mga observable na sinusukat, at (2) isaalang-alang ang malamang na epekto ng mga error sa circuit, at bawiin ang mga ito sa pamamagitan ng pagsukat ng ibang observable. Gumagamit ang susunod na dalawang tool ng mga approach na ito.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Operator backpropagation {#operator-backpropagation}"
msgstr "Operator backpropagation {#operator-backpropagation}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Operator backpropagation](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-addon-obp) reduces circuit depth by absorbing gates from the end of a circuit into the measured observable. For example, consider the following circuit.\n"
msgstr "Binabawasan ng [Operator backpropagation](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-addon-obp) ang depth ng circuit sa pamamagitan ng pagsipsip ng mga gate mula sa dulo ng circuit sa sinusukat na observable. Halimbawa, isaalang-alang ang sumusunod na circuit.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![An image showing a quantum circuit with several entangling and rotation layers, followed by a ladder of CNOTs from qubit 0 down to qubit 5. Finally, a Z measurement is made on qubit 5.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/modern-workflows/backprop.avif)\n"
msgstr "![An image showing a quantum circuit with several entangling and rotation layers, followed by a ladder of CNOTs from qubit 0 down to qubit 5. Finally, a Z measurement is made on qubit 5.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/modern-workflows/backprop.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This circuit contains rotation and entangling layers that appear nontrivial, followed by a ladder of CNOT gates and a measurement of `Z` on qubit 5. This circuit has a two-qubit depth of 7. This depth is before transpilation. In practice, you typically apply backpropagation after transpilation, but this example is for teaching purposes only. Recall that there are rules for propagating an observable past a gate. In particular, when a CNOT gate has target $q_t$ and control $q_c$, a $Z_t$ observable on $q_t$ becomes $Z_c Z_t$ when propagated backward past the CNOT gate: $Z_t \\rightarrow Z_c Z_t$. In this example circuit, if you propagate the observable $Z_5$ back through the entire ladder of CNOT gates, you get the observable $Z_5 Z_4 Z_3 Z_2 Z_1 Z_0$, or in standard Qiskit notation, simply $ZZZZZZ$. If we measure this observable instead of only $Z_5$, we can remove the entire ladder of CNOT gates, which reduces the two-qubit depth from 7 to 2. This observable still requires a measurement in only one basis on each qubit, so it does not increase the number of shots that we require. This is not always the case. Generally, more complicated observables require more shots, and sometimes more measurements in different bases.\n"
msgstr "Naglalaman ang circuit na ito ng mga rotation at entangling layer na mukhang hindi simple, na sinusundan ng isang ladder ng mga CNOT gate at isang pagsukat ng `Z` sa qubit 5. May two-qubit depth na 7 ang circuit na ito. Ang depth na ito ay bago ang transpilation. Sa praktika, karaniwan mong inilalapat ang backpropagation pagkatapos ng transpilation, ngunit para sa layuning pang-turo lamang ang halimbawang ito. Tandaan na may mga patakaran para sa pag-propagate ng isang observable lampas sa isang gate. Partikular, kapag ang isang CNOT gate ay may target na $q_t$ at control na $q_c$, ang isang observable na $Z_t$ sa $q_t$ ay nagiging $Z_c Z_t$ kapag na-propagate pabalik lampas sa CNOT gate: $Z_t \\rightarrow Z_c Z_t$. Sa halimbawang circuit na ito, kung i-propagate mo ang observable na $Z_5$ pabalik sa buong ladder ng mga CNOT gate, makukuha mo ang observable na $Z_5 Z_4 Z_3 Z_2 Z_1 Z_0$, o sa karaniwang notasyon ng Qiskit, simpleng $ZZZZZZ$. Kung susukatin natin ang observable na ito sa halip na $Z_5$ lamang, maaari nating alisin ang buong ladder ng mga CNOT gate, na nagbabawas sa two-qubit depth mula 7 tungong 2. Nangangailangan pa rin ang observable na ito ng pagsukat sa isang basis lamang sa bawat qubit, kaya hindi nito dinadagdagan ang bilang ng mga shot na kailangan natin. Hindi ito laging ganito. Sa pangkalahatan, mas maraming shot ang kailangan ng mas masalimuot na mga observable, at minsan mas maraming pagsukat sa iba't ibang basis.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The overall strategy of operator backpropagation includes the following steps:\n"
msgstr "Kasama sa pangkalahatang estratehiya ng operator backpropagation ang mga sumusunod na hakbang:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Shorten the executed circuit\n"
msgstr "Paikliin ang isinasagawang circuit\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Replace the original observable with an expanded observable\n"
msgstr "Palitan ang orihinal na observable ng pinalawak na observable\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Trade circuit depth for increased sampling requirements\n"
msgstr "Ipagpalit ang depth ng circuit sa dagdag na pangangailangan sa sampling\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The previous circuit is an obvious example in which backpropagation is advantageous. In general, however, it is not easy to identify the circuits that benefit most from backpropagation. To decide when to use backpropagation, check how much depth you can remove from your circuit, and weigh that reduction against the increased sampling requirements.\n"
msgstr "Malinaw na halimbawa ang naunang circuit kung saan kapaki-pakinabang ang backpropagation. Sa pangkalahatan, gayunpaman, hindi madaling tukuyin ang mga circuit na pinakamaraming makukuhang pakinabang sa backpropagation. Para magpasya kung kailan gagamit ng backpropagation, tingnan kung gaano karaming depth ang maaalis mo sa iyong circuit, at timbangin ang pagbabawas na iyon laban sa dagdag na pangangailangan sa sampling.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Propagated noise absorption (PNA) {#propagated-noise-absorption-pna}"
msgstr "Propagated noise absorption (PNA) {#propagated-noise-absorption-pna}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Propagated noise absorption](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-addon-pna) is structurally similar to operator backpropagation. However, instead of propagating an operator back through the ideal gates in a circuit, PNA incorporates a learned noise model and propagates the effects of noise directly into the observable. PNA does the following:\n"
msgstr "Katulad ang [Propagated noise absorption](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-addon-pna) sa istruktura ng operator backpropagation. Gayunpaman, sa halip na i-propagate ang isang operator pabalik sa mga ideal na gate sa isang circuit, isinasama ng PNA ang isang natutunang noise model at direktang ipino-propagate ang mga epekto ng noise sa observable. Ginagawa ng PNA ang sumusunod:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Learns noise behavior from the hardware\n"
msgstr "Natututo ng noise behavior mula sa hardware\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Propagates the noise model through the circuit\n"
msgstr "Ipino-propagate ang noise model sa circuit\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Produces a modified observable that compensates for gate noise\n"
msgstr "Gumagawa ng binagong observable na bumabawi sa gate noise\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![An image showing the gate errors on many layers of a quantum circuit being propagated forward to the final observable measurement.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/modern-workflows/pna.avif)\n"
msgstr "![An image showing the gate errors on many layers of a quantum circuit being propagated forward to the final observable measurement.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/modern-workflows/pna.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When the modified observable is measured on noisy hardware, the resulting expectation values better approximate the ideal noiseless result. PNA has two types of overhead. First, you must learn the noise model, which requires running additional circuits. Second, PNA can produce more complicated observables, which can increase sampling requirements.\n"
msgstr "Kapag sinukat ang binagong observable sa maingay na hardware, mas lumalapit ang mga nagreresultang expectation value sa ideal na resultang walang noise. May dalawang uri ng overhead ang PNA. Una, kailangan mong matutunan ang noise model, na nangangailangan ng pagpapatakbo ng mga karagdagang circuit. Pangalawa, maaaring gumawa ang PNA ng mas masalimuot na mga observable, na maaaring magpataas ng pangangailangan sa sampling.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Circuit cutting {#circuit-cutting}"
msgstr "Circuit cutting {#circuit-cutting}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Circuit cutting](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-cutting/) partitions a large circuit into smaller subcircuits that can run independently. You then make enough measurements to recombine the results. Circuit cutting does the following:\n"
msgstr "Hinahati ng [Circuit cutting](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-cutting/) ang isang malaking circuit sa mas maliliit na subcircuit na maaaring tumakbo nang magkakahiwalay. Pagkatapos ay gumagawa ka ng sapat na mga pagsukat para pagsamahin muli ang mga resulta. Ginagawa ng circuit cutting ang sumusunod:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Reduces hardware requirements\n"
msgstr "Binabawasan ang mga pangangailangan sa hardware\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Allows computations larger than available qubit counts (wider circuits)\n"
msgstr "Nagpapahintulot ng mga computation na mas malaki kaysa sa available na bilang ng qubit (mas malalapad na circuit)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Helps address depth and connectivity limitations (deeper circuits)\n"
msgstr "Tumutulong tugunan ang mga limitasyon sa depth at connectivity (mas malalalim na circuit)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Reconstructs the original result through classical post-processing\n"
msgstr "Binubuo muli ang orihinal na resulta sa pamamagitan ng classical na post-processing\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![An image showing two circuits being cut, so that they can be run separately and recombined later in post-processing.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/modern-workflows/cutting.avif)\n"
msgstr "![An image showing two circuits being cut, so that they can be run separately and recombined later in post-processing.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/modern-workflows/cutting.avif)\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Samplomatic {#samplomatic}"
msgstr "Samplomatic {#samplomatic}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Many of the techniques in the previous sections complement other suppression and mitigation methods covered throughout this course, including:\n"
msgstr "Marami sa mga technique sa mga naunang seksyon ay umaakma sa iba pang paraan ng suppression at mitigation na tinalakay sa buong kursong ito, kabilang ang:\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Dynamical decoupling\n"
msgstr "Dynamical decoupling\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pauli twirling\n"
msgstr "Pauli twirling\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "M3\n"
msgstr "M3\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "TREX\n"
msgstr "TREX\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Zero-noise extrapolation (ZNE)\n"
msgstr "Zero-noise extrapolation (ZNE)\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Probabilistic error cancellation (PEC)\n"
msgstr "Probabilistic error cancellation (PEC)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In many workflows, you can apply different techniques to different regions of the same circuit. As we have seen, many of these techniques also come with quantum overhead. We therefore sometimes need fine, detailed control over noise learning, sampling, and the application of twirling sequences. These are some of the motivations behind Samplomatic.\n"
msgstr "Sa maraming workflow, maaari kang maglapat ng iba't ibang technique sa iba't ibang rehiyon ng iisang circuit. Tulad ng nakita natin, may kasamang quantum overhead ang marami sa mga technique na ito. Kaya minsan kailangan natin ng pino at detalyadong kontrol sa noise learning, sampling, at paglalapat ng mga twirling sequence. Ito ang ilan sa mga motibasyon sa likod ng Samplomatic.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Samplomatic](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/samplomatic) is an open-source library that enables customized sampling, randomization, and error-mitigation workflows.\n"
msgstr "Ang [Samplomatic](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/samplomatic) ay isang open-source na library na nagbibigay-daan sa customized na sampling, randomization, at mga workflow ng error-mitigation.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Its first task is to analyze a circuit and divide it into labeled regions, or boxes. These boxes serve two purposes:\n"
msgstr "Ang unang gawain nito ay suriin ang isang circuit at hatiin ito sa mga may-label na rehiyon, o box. May dalawang layunin ang mga box na ito:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "They visually partition the circuit.\n"
msgstr "Biswal nilang hinahati ang circuit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "They create indexed regions that can be configured independently.\n"
msgstr "Gumagawa sila ng mga naka-index na rehiyon na maaaring i-configure nang hiwalay.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Users can attach annotations that describe how each box should be treated during execution. Examples include:\n"
msgstr "Maaaring maglakip ang mga user ng mga annotation na naglalarawan kung paano dapat tratuhin ang bawat box habang nag-eexecute. Kabilang sa mga halimbawa ang:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Applying Pauli twirling to all boxes\n"
msgstr "Paglalapat ng Pauli twirling sa lahat ng box\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Applying twirling only to selected boxes\n"
msgstr "Paglalapat ng twirling sa mga napiling box lamang\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Using different twirling groups in different regions\n"
msgstr "Paggamit ng iba't ibang twirling group sa iba't ibang rehiyon\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Injecting learned noise into specific layers\n"
msgstr "Pag-inject ng natutunang noise sa mga partikular na layer\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Customizing mitigation strategies at a fine-grained level\n"
msgstr "Pag-customize ng mga estratehiya sa mitigation sa napakadetalyadong antas\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Samplomatic also identifies repeated boxed regions. Because identical layers typically exhibit similar noise characteristics, you only need to perform noise learning once for each unique layer.\n"
msgstr "Kinikilala rin ng Samplomatic ang mga paulit-ulit na boxed na rehiyon. Dahil karaniwang magkakapareho ang katangian ng noise ng magkakaparehong layer, kailangan mo lang gawin ang noise learning nang isang beses para sa bawat natatanging layer.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Samplomatic outputs {#samplomatic-outputs}"
msgstr "Mga output ng Samplomatic {#samplomatic-outputs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Samplomatic produces two primary objects:\n"
msgstr "Dalawang pangunahing object ang nililikha ng Samplomatic:\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Template circuit\n"
msgstr "Template circuit\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Samplex\n"
msgstr "Samplex\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The template circuit is a boxed, transpiled, parameterized circuit that is ready for execution. The samplex contains all the information that is required to generate and process circuit variants. Samplex contents include:\n"
msgstr "Ang template circuit ay isang boxed, transpiled, at parameterized na circuit na handa nang i-execute. Taglay ng samplex ang lahat ng impormasyong kailangan para makabuo at magproseso ng mga variant ng circuit. Kasama sa laman ng samplex ang mga sumusunod:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Parameter values for parameterized circuits\n"
msgstr "Mga halaga ng parameter para sa mga parameterized na circuit\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Randomization selections\n"
msgstr "Mga napiling randomization\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sampling distributions\n"
msgstr "Mga sampling distribution\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Post-processing information\n"
msgstr "Impormasyon para sa post-processing\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Additional execution metadata\n"
msgstr "Karagdagang metadata ng execution\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Formally, a samplex is a probability distribution over the parameters of a template circuit, together with auxiliary information that is required for execution and post-processing. An important practical advantage is that both the template circuit and the samplex are created locally on the client side. As a result, you can inspect, validate, and debug them before you use any hardware resources.\n"
msgstr "Pormal na pagsasabi, ang samplex ay isang probability distribution sa mga parameter ng isang template circuit, kasama ang karagdagang impormasyong kailangan para sa execution at post-processing. Isang mahalagang praktikal na bentahe na parehong nililikha nang lokal sa client side ang template circuit at ang samplex. Dahil dito, maaari mo silang suriin, i-validate, at i-debug bago ka gumamit ng anumang hardware resource.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Samplomatic has many benefits, including fine-grained control of adaptive shot allocation and randomization. It also has logistical benefits, such as structured post-processing workflows. One of the most important benefits is the reuse of learned noise information across identical layers, which can save a significant amount of quantum computing time during noise learning.\n"
msgstr "Maraming benepisyo ang Samplomatic, kabilang ang napakadetalyadong kontrol sa adaptive shot allocation at randomization. May mga benepisyo rin ito sa lohistika, tulad ng mga structured na workflow sa post-processing. Isa sa pinakamahalagang benepisyo ang muling paggamit ng natutunang impormasyon tungkol sa noise sa magkakaparehong layer, na makakatipid ng malaking oras sa quantum computing habang nag-noise learning.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Shaded lightcones {#shaded-lightcones}"
msgstr "Shaded lightcones {#shaded-lightcones}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Before you decide where to apply expensive mitigation techniques, it is helpful to identify the regions of a circuit that matter most to the observable that is being measured. This need motivates the [shaded lightcones](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-addon-slc) addon. The idea of a lightcone comes from relativity, in which causal relationships are constrained by the finite speed at which information can travel.\n"
msgstr "Bago ka magpasya kung saan ilalapat ang mamahaling mga teknik sa mitigation, nakakatulong na tukuyin ang mga rehiyon ng circuit na pinakamahalaga sa observable na sinusukat. Ito ang dahilan ng addon na [shaded lightcones](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-addon-slc). Ang ideya ng lightcone ay galing sa relativity, kung saan nililimitahan ng may hangganang bilis ng paglalakbay ng impormasyon ang mga ugnayang sanhi.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![An image of spacetime. Time runs from bottom to top, and space runs from side to side. Because no causation can move through space faster than the speed of light, the region of spacetime that an event can causally influence is limited to a conical region. This is an analogy for the spreading of errors in a quantum circuit.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/modern-workflows/lightcone.avif)\n"
msgstr "![An image of spacetime. Time runs from bottom to top, and space runs from side to side. Because no causation can move through space faster than the speed of light, the region of spacetime that an event can causally influence is limited to a conical region. This is an analogy for the spreading of errors in a quantum circuit.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/modern-workflows/lightcone.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A similar concept applies in quantum circuits.\n"
msgstr "May katulad na konsepto sa mga quantum circuit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Consider a large circuit in which only a low-weight observable is of interest. A low-weight observable acts nontrivially on only a few qubits. Low-weight observables are of interest for many reasons. For example, they can represent the following:\n"
msgstr "Isipin ang isang malaking circuit na ang interesado ka lang ay isang low-weight na observable. Ang low-weight na observable ay kumikilos nang hindi trivial sa ilang qubit lang. Interesado ang marami sa mga low-weight na observable sa iba't ibang dahilan. Halimbawa, maaari silang kumatawan sa mga sumusunod:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Individual terms within a larger Hamiltonian\n"
msgstr "Mga indibidwal na term sa loob ng mas malaking Hamiltonian\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A localized interaction region\n"
msgstr "Isang naka-localize na rehiyon ng interaksyon\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Information collected onto a small set of ancilla qubits\n"
msgstr "Impormasyong naipon sa maliit na hanay ng mga ancilla qubit\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Other observables that involve only a few qubits\n"
msgstr "Iba pang observable na may kinalaman sa ilang qubit lang\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Not every error in the circuit can affect the measurement outcome. This is especially true of Pauli errors, or any error that can be modeled as a set of Pauli operations. For example, look at the following circuit:\n"
msgstr "Hindi lahat ng error sa circuit ay makakaapekto sa resulta ng pagsukat. Totoo ito lalo na sa mga Pauli error, o anumang error na maaaring i-model bilang hanay ng mga Pauli operation. Halimbawa, tingnan ang sumusunod na circuit:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A quantum circuit with an error on qubit 0 just before measurement. A measurement is performed only on qubit 6, and there is no entangling gate between qubits 0 and 6 in the final layer.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/modern-workflows/lightcone-a.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A quantum circuit with an error on qubit 0 just before measurement. A measurement is performed only on qubit 6, and there is no entangling gate between qubits 0 and 6 in the final layer.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/modern-workflows/lightcone-a.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A Pauli error on qubit 0 in the final layer cannot influence the measurement on qubit 6, because there is no connecting gate that could propagate the error from qubit 0 to qubit 6. Note that this argument does not apply to certain non-unitary errors. For example, a T1-like transition to the ground state on qubit 0 collapses qubit 0 to a computational basis state. If qubits 0 and 6 were previously entangled (as they are in this circuit), the non-unitary error on qubit 0 can affect qubit 6. The following discussion focuses on errors that can be represented as Pauli operations, or as probabilistic mixtures of Pauli operations.\n"
msgstr "Hindi maaapektuhan ng Pauli error sa qubit 0 sa huling layer ang pagsukat sa qubit 6, dahil walang nag-uugnay na gate na maaaring magpalaganap ng error mula qubit 0 papunta sa qubit 6. Tandaan na hindi ito naaangkop sa ilang non-unitary na error. Halimbawa, ang T1-like na transition papunta sa ground state sa qubit 0 ay nagko-collapse sa qubit 0 sa isang computational basis state. Kung dating entangled ang qubit 0 at 6 (gaya sa circuit na ito), maaaring maapektuhan ng non-unitary na error sa qubit 0 ang qubit 6. Nakatuon ang sumusunod na talakayan sa mga error na maaaring katawanin bilang mga Pauli operation, o bilang probabilistic na halo ng mga Pauli operation.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the last layer, only a Pauli error on qubit 5 or qubit 6 can directly affect the measurement on qubit 6.\n"
msgstr "Sa huling layer, tanging ang Pauli error sa qubit 5 o qubit 6 ang direktang makakaapekto sa pagsukat sa qubit 6.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the entangling layer before that one, qubits 5 and 6 are entangled with qubits 4 and 7, respectively. Therefore, in that entangling layer or just before it, a Pauli error on any of those four qubits can affect the later measurement. You can continue to trace backward through the circuit to find the subset of gates and qubits that are causally connected to the measurement. This causal set forms a cone-shaped region in space (qubits) and time (layers), which gives rise to the term lightcone. The exact shape of the region varies from circuit to circuit. Because this analysis depends on hardware connectivity and gate placement, it is most useful after transpilation, routing, and layout optimization.\n"
msgstr "Sa entangling layer bago nito, naka-entangle ang qubit 5 at 6 sa qubit 4 at 7, ayon sa pagkakasunod. Kaya sa entangling layer na iyon o bago lang nito, maaaring makaapekto sa susunod na pagsukat ang Pauli error sa alinman sa apat na qubit na iyon. Maaari mong ipagpatuloy ang pagsubaybay pabalik sa circuit para mahanap ang subset ng mga gate at qubit na may ugnayang sanhi sa pagsukat. Bumubuo ang sanhing hanay na ito ng rehiyong hugis-cone sa espasyo (mga qubit) at oras (mga layer), kaya tinawag itong lightcone. Iba-iba ang eksaktong hugis ng rehiyon sa bawat circuit. Dahil nakasalalay ang pagsusuring ito sa hardware connectivity at paglalagay ng gate, pinakamakatulong ito pagkatapos ng transpilation, routing, at layout optimization.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Beyond causal connectivity {#beyond-causal-connectivity}"
msgstr "Higit pa sa causal connectivity {#beyond-causal-connectivity}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Shaded lightcones extend this idea by also considering which types of errors matter.\n"
msgstr "Pinalalawak ng shaded lightcones ang ideyang ito sa pamamagitan din ng pagsasaalang-alang kung anong mga uri ng error ang mahalaga.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For example, note the following:\n"
msgstr "Halimbawa, tandaan ang mga sumusunod:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A Z error immediately before a Z-basis measurement has no effect on the measurement outcome.\n"
msgstr "Walang epekto sa resulta ng pagsukat ang Z error bago mismo ang Z-basis na pagsukat.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "An X error immediately before a Z-basis measurement can dramatically change the result.\n"
msgstr "Maaaring baguhin nang malaki ang resulta ng X error bago mismo ang Z-basis na pagsukat.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Some error types therefore deserve more mitigation effort than others. This distinction can substantially reduce the overhead of techniques such as PEC. In practice, the addon generates separate sensitivity analyses for each of the following error types:\n"
msgstr "Kaya may mga uri ng error na nangangailangan ng mas maraming pagsisikap sa mitigation kaysa sa iba. Malaki ang naibabawas ng pagkakaibang ito sa overhead ng mga teknik tulad ng PEC. Sa praktika, gumagawa ang addon ng hiwalay na sensitivity analysis para sa bawat isa sa mga sumusunod na uri ng error:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "X errors\n"
msgstr "X errors\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Z errors\n"
msgstr "Z errors\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Y (or XZ up to a phase) errors\n"
msgstr "Mga Y error (o XZ hanggang sa phase)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This error sensitivity generally looks different for each error type, because different causally connected errors have different impacts on the measurement. Note also that the sensitivity changes throughout the circuit. An X error immediately before measurement might be highly damaging, while an error that occurs many layers earlier might have a smaller effect after it propagates through a highly entangled state.\n"
msgstr "Karaniwang magkakaiba ang hitsura ng error sensitivity na ito para sa bawat uri ng error, dahil magkakaiba ang epekto ng mga error na may ugnayang sanhi sa pagsukat. Tandaan din na nagbabago ang sensitivity sa buong circuit. Ang X error bago mismo ang pagsukat ay maaaring lubhang nakakasira, habang ang error na nangyari ilang layer na ang nakaraan ay maaaring mas maliit ang epekto matapos itong kumalat sa isang lubhang entangled na estado.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Three images showing the same quantum circuit, but with (a) no error, (b) an error just before measurement, and (c) an error earlier in the circuit.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/modern-workflows/sensitivity.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Three images showing the same quantum circuit, but with (a) no error, (b) an error just before measurement, and (c) an error earlier in the circuit.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/modern-workflows/sensitivity.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Shaded lightcones quantify this difference by assigning a sensitivity value to potential errors throughout the circuit.\n"
msgstr "Kinukwantipika ng shaded lightcones ang pagkakaibang ito sa pamamagitan ng pagtatalaga ng sensitivity value sa mga posibleng error sa buong circuit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The resulting maps indicate the following:\n"
msgstr "Ipinapakita ng mga resultang mapa ang mga sumusunod:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Where errors matter\n"
msgstr "Kung saan mahalaga ang mga error\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Which error types matter\n"
msgstr "Kung aling mga uri ng error ang mahalaga\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "How strongly they influence the final observable\n"
msgstr "Gaano kalakas ang impluwensya nila sa huling observable\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Three images showing heat maps of error sensitivity to three different error types: X, Y, and Z.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/modern-workflows/slc-xyz.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Three images showing heat maps of error sensitivity to three different error types: X, Y, and Z.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/modern-workflows/slc-xyz.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Shaded lightcones do not mitigate errors themselves, but they can help focus mitigation effort where it provides the greatest benefit.\n"
msgstr "Hindi mismo nagmi-mitigate ng mga error ang shaded lightcones, pero makakatulong ang mga ito na itutok ang pagsisikap sa mitigation kung saan pinakamalaki ang benepisyo.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Learn and inject noise {#learn-and-inject-noise}"
msgstr "Mag-learn at mag-inject ng noise {#learn-and-inject-noise}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "After a circuit has been constructed, optimized, and annotated, two complementary tasks remain: learning the noise, and using the noise model (for example, to inject noise or to propagate the effects of noise).\n"
msgstr "Matapos mabuo, ma-optimize, at ma-annotate ang isang circuit, may dalawang magkaagapay na gawaing natitira: ang pag-learn ng noise, at ang paggamit ng noise model (halimbawa, para mag-inject ng noise o magpalaganap ng mga epekto ng noise).\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "NoiseLearnerV3 {#noiselearnerv3}"
msgstr "NoiseLearnerV3 {#noiselearnerv3}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "NoiseLearnerV3 is the current tool for noise learning. The previous NoiseLearner interface accepted entire circuits and produced Pauli-Lindblad noise models. NoiseLearnerV3 instead operates directly on boxed circuit instructions. In summary, NoiseLearnerV3 does the following:\n"
msgstr "Ang NoiseLearnerV3 ang kasalukuyang tool para sa noise learning. Ang naunang interface na NoiseLearner ay tumatanggap ng buong circuit at gumagawa ng mga Pauli-Lindblad noise model. Sa halip, direktang gumagana ang NoiseLearnerV3 sa mga boxed na circuit instruction. Sa madaling sabi, ginagawa ng NoiseLearnerV3 ang mga sumusunod:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Accepts collections of labeled circuit layers\n"
msgstr "Tumatanggap ng mga koleksyon ng may-label na circuit layer\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Reuses information from repeated layers\n"
msgstr "Muling ginagamit ang impormasyon mula sa mga paulit-ulit na layer\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Supports measurement-noise learning\n"
msgstr "Sumusuporta sa pag-learn ng measurement noise\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Supports post-processing of learned models\n"
msgstr "Sumusuporta sa post-processing ng mga natutunang model\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Enables noise injection and scaling workflows\n"
msgstr "Nagbibigay-daan sa mga workflow ng noise injection at scaling\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This design aligns closely with the layer-oriented workflow of Samplomatic. In particular, NoiseLearnerV3 uses the following methods for each instruction set:\n"
msgstr "Malapit na umaayon ang disenyong ito sa layer-oriented na workflow ng Samplomatic. Sa partikular, ginagamit ng NoiseLearnerV3 ang mga sumusunod na paraan para sa bawat instruction set:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pauli-Lindblad learning for gate operations\n"
msgstr "Pauli-Lindblad learning para sa mga gate operation\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "TREX-based learning for measurements\n"
msgstr "TREX-based na learning para sa mga pagsukat\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can then use a learned noise model in many of the methods that we have already covered. For example, recall that zero-noise extrapolation (ZNE) with gate folding can lead to intractably deep circuits. The alternative method for scaling noise in that case was to sample from a known noise model, which effectively increases the noise level, even by non-integer factors. This method, probabilistic error amplification (PEA), is a good example of how you can use a noise model to mitigate errors. A good noise model is also required for probabilistic error cancellation (PEC) and propagated noise absorption (PNA).\n"
msgstr "Maaari mo nang gamitin ang natutunang noise model sa maraming paraang napag-usapan na natin. Halimbawa, tandaan na ang zero-noise extrapolation (ZNE) na may gate folding ay maaaring humantong sa mga circuit na napakalalim na hindi na kayang gawin. Ang alternatibong paraan para i-scale ang noise sa kasong iyon ay ang pag-sample mula sa kilalang noise model, na epektibong nagpapataas ng antas ng noise, kahit sa mga hindi buong salik. Ang paraang ito, ang probabilistic error amplification (PEA), ay magandang halimbawa kung paano mo magagamit ang noise model para i-mitigate ang mga error. Kailangan din ang mahusay na noise model para sa probabilistic error cancellation (PEC) at propagated noise absorption (PNA).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In short, with a high-quality noise model, noise becomes a programmable resource rather than only a source of error.\n"
msgstr "Sa madaling sabi, sa mataas na kalidad na noise model, nagiging programmable na resource ang noise sa halip na pinagmumulan lang ng error.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Shaded lightcones versus NoiseLearnerV3 {#shaded-lightcones-versus-noiselearnerv3}"
msgstr "Shaded lightcones laban sa NoiseLearnerV3 {#shaded-lightcones-versus-noiselearnerv3}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "NoiseLearnerV3 and SLC are closely related, but they take distinct inputs and answer different questions. SLC determines where to focus mitigation effort. NoiseLearnerV3 characterizes the actual noise present in those regions. These processes also involve different kinds of overhead. The following table summarizes these differences.\n"
msgstr "Magkaugnay na mabuti ang NoiseLearnerV3 at SLC, pero magkaiba ang mga input nila at iba ang mga tanong na sinasagot. Tinutukoy ng SLC kung saan itutuon ang pagsisikap sa mitigation. Tinutukoy naman ng NoiseLearnerV3 ang aktwal na noise sa mga rehiyong iyon. Magkaiba rin ang uri ng overhead ng dalawang prosesong ito. Binubuod ng sumusunod na talahanayan ang mga pagkakaibang ito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"|   | Shaded lightcones | NoiseLearnerV3 |\n"
"|---|-------------------|----------------|\n"
"| Purpose | Identifies where mitigation matters | Learns how errors behave |\n"
"| Overhead | Primarily classical overhead | Requires hardware executions |\n"
"| Output | Produces sensitivity maps | Produces noise-channel descriptions |\n"
"| Input | Uses circuit structure and operator propagation | Uses circuit structure and experimental hardware data |\n"
msgstr ""
"|   | Shaded lightcones | NoiseLearnerV3 |\n"
"|---|-------------------|----------------|\n"
"| Layunin | Tinutukoy kung saan mahalaga ang mitigation | Inaaral kung paano kumikilos ang mga error |\n"
"| Overhead | Pangunahing classical na overhead | Nangangailangan ng mga hardware execution |\n"
"| Output | Gumagawa ng mga sensitivity map | Gumagawa ng mga paglalarawan ng noise channel |\n"
"| Input | Gumagamit ng istruktura ng circuit at operator propagation | Gumagamit ng istruktura ng circuit at eksperimental na hardware data |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Executor and runtime execution {#executor-and-runtime-execution}"
msgstr "Executor at runtime execution {#executor-and-runtime-execution}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Executor performs the final execution step. It can operate on either of the following inputs:\n"
msgstr "Ginagawa ng Executor ang huling hakbang ng execution. Maaari itong gumana sa alinman sa mga sumusunod na input:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A template circuit and samplex generated by Samplomatic\n"
msgstr "Isang template circuit at samplex na nilikha ng Samplomatic\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A conventional quantum circuit without Samplomatic\n"
msgstr "Isang karaniwang quantum circuit na walang Samplomatic\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "With this flexibility, you can adopt as many or as few components of the directed execution workflow as you need.\n"
msgstr "Dahil sa kakayahang umangkop na ito, maaari kang gumamit ng kasing dami o kasing konti ng mga bahagi ng directed execution workflow ayon sa kailangan mo.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Executor works closely with Samplomatic, which manages randomization choices, shot allocation, noise-injection selections, and related execution metadata, as described previously.\n"
msgstr "Malapit na gumagana ang Executor kasama ng Samplomatic, na namamahala sa mga pagpili sa randomization, shot allocation, mga pagpili sa noise-injection, at kaugnay na metadata ng execution, gaya ng inilarawan kanina.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For practical examples of the directed execution model, see the [Directed execution model](/guides/directed-execution-model) guide as well as the [tutorials](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/tutorials) and [Qiskit addon documentation](/guides/addons) on [IBM Quantum&reg; Platform](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/).\n"
msgstr "Para sa mga praktikal na halimbawa ng directed execution model, tingnan ang gabay na [Directed execution model](/guides/directed-execution-model) pati na rin ang mga [tutorial](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/tutorials) at [dokumentasyon ng Qiskit addon](/guides/addons) sa [IBM Quantum&reg; Platform](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/).\n"

